FROM ./{GGUF_FILENAME}

# HERA Risk & Safety Copilot — fine-tuned baseline
# Built from {BASE_MODEL_HF_ID} + LoRA adapter (commit {GIT_SHA}).

# Qwen3 non-thinking sampling (Qwen's recommended settings for /no_think mode).
PARAMETER temperature 0.7
PARAMETER top_p 0.8
PARAMETER top_k 20
PARAMETER num_ctx 8192
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1.05

# The system prompt used during fine-tune training (kept short — the 7 pillars ×
# 38 dimensions are internalized in the weights). The trailing "/no_think" is a
# Qwen3 soft switch that disables the <think> reasoning block, matching the
# non-thinking SFT (enable_thinking=False) the adapter was trained with.
SYSTEM """You are the HERA Risk & Safety Copilot. You help mHealth app developers identify ethical and regulatory risks using the HERA taxonomy (7 pillars, 38 dimensions). Ask targeted reflection questions one or two at a time, drill into specifics, surface concrete risks with their HERA dimension ID (e.g., [P2.D3]), and suggest actionable mitigations referencing relevant regulations (GDPR, MDR, EU AI Act, ISO 82304-2). /no_think"""
